WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:06.300
This Ryan Reynolds movie died an early death when&nbsp;
it hit theaters. But after years spent lying in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.174
a cinematic grave, it's getting resurrected&nbsp;
for a second shot at the big time on Netflix.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.600
While Ryan Reynolds has starred in some&nbsp;
well-received movies like "Deadpool," "Free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.000
Guy," and "Waiting...," his career includes a&nbsp;
few box office misfires as well. Nevertheless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.980
his career seems relatively unshakable with&nbsp;
years and years as a leading man. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.460
appearing in several television&nbsp;
series and TV movies early on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.900
Reynolds got his first big break with&nbsp;
"National Lampoon's Van Wilder," in which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.677
he plays a fast talking scamp that doesn't&nbsp;
play by the rules. Sounds familiar, no?

00:00:38.677 --> 00:00:42.372
"You think Ryan Reynolds got this&nbsp;
far on his superior acting method?"

00:00:42.372 --> 00:00:47.040
Possible pigeon-holing aside, Reynolds is&nbsp;
certainly popular these days, bolstered by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.360
his excitement around playing Marvel's Merc&nbsp;
with a Mouth, his constant back and forth on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.400
social media with his famous wife Blake Lively,&nbsp;
and his cell phone service company Mint Mobile.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.325
Reynolds is a star outside of&nbsp;
major franchise releases too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.325 --> 00:01:06.360
including in Apple TV+'s "Spirited," a Reynolds&nbsp;
and Will Ferrell Christmastime team-up. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.620
it seems that Reynolds' present day popularity&nbsp;
is breathing life into one of his older films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.520
and one that certainly qualified as a&nbsp;
flop when it was originally released.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.900
Currently, Ryan Reynolds's "R.I.P.D." is&nbsp;
apparently attracting the attention of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.100
considerable number of viewers online,&nbsp;
landing it at the top of Netflix's Top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.880
10 list. "R.I.P.D." originally&nbsp;
premiered in theaters back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:33.001
2013 and stars Reynolds and Jeff Bridges as&nbsp;
supernatural cops. Remind you of anything?

00:01:33.109 --> 00:01:34.369
"Who're you meeting?"

00:01:34.369 --> 00:01:35.317
"Well, it's a ship."

00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:38.000
"A ship? I didn't see a&nbsp;
departure clearance for today."

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.420
R.I.P.D.'s light twist on a well-worn&nbsp;
genre trope is that the cops are both dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.320
and now exist as phantoms in the&nbsp;
world of the living. Their jobs as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.460
undead specters see them tasked with hunting&nbsp;
down other dead people who remain at large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:55.740
attempting to duck the afterlife. This means that&nbsp;
Reynolds and Bridges' characters can manifest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.652
in the physical world in different bodies,&nbsp;
but with the caveat that they cannot reveal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:04.092
their true nature to civilians. Of course, this&nbsp;
becomes a source of comedy throughout the film.

00:02:04.092 --> 00:02:07.440
"I'm not a piece of meat put on&nbsp;
this earth for your gratification,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.700
I'm a woman. Respect me or I will&nbsp;
castrate you like a three year old steer."

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:18.180
However, it seemed like the critics weren't&nbsp;
laughing. Despite an all-star cast comprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:24.120
of cinematic powerhouses like Reynolds, Bridges,&nbsp;
Kevin Bacon, and Mary-Louise Parker, critics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.500
weren't kind to the film in reviews published&nbsp;
around the time of its release. Likewise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:35.400
the movie didn't perform well at the box office,&nbsp;
earning $79 million against a $130 million budget.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.360
Beyond Reynolds' growing presence in&nbsp;
the present day pop cultural zeitgeist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:45.060
the resurrection of "R.I.P.D." as a hit on Netflix&nbsp;
seems to simply be the result of the film joining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:50.880
the streaming service's catalog at the start of&nbsp;
March 2023. Nevertheless, its sudden and sharp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.920
rise in popularity is all the more surprising when&nbsp;
taking into account what critics had to say about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:02.100
the film in contemporaneous reviews. For example,&nbsp;
RogerEbert.com writer Steven Boone awarded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:08.449
"R.I.P.D." one star, and concluded his review&nbsp;
by stating, quote, "It's an awful, awful film."
 &nbsp;

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:09.960
"This is a joke."

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.340
Meanwhile, for The Guardian, Mark Kermode&nbsp;
rated the film two-out-of-five stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.353
and criticized its lack of&nbsp;
a proper reason to exist.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:21.300
"Overall, it's a directionless&nbsp;
mess: too expensive for a B-movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.680
too grown-up for a kids' movie (funerals,&nbsp;
bereavement and jokes about Steely Dan)&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.481
and too infantile for everyone else. No&nbsp;
wonder it died on its feet in the US."

00:03:30.481 --> 00:03:35.820
That said, its addition to Netflix is, at&nbsp;
least, unsurprising. Near the end of 2022, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:41.160
prequel — with none of the original cast returning&nbsp;
— titled "R.I.P.D. 2: Rise of the Damned" became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:46.320
available to Netflix subscribers. Of course, for&nbsp;
Reynolds' fanbase, quality or the existence of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:51.360
a sequel may even be beside the point. Rather,&nbsp;
easy access to a new Reynolds film seems to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.677
been enough of a reason to make what was once a&nbsp;
major theatrical flop into a streaming success.

